<div className="space-y-5">
<h3 id="coastal-bird-photography-in-morocco" className="scroll-mt-28 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl">Coastal Bird Photography in Morocco</h3>
<div className="mt-5 space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-8 text-slate-700">
<p>Coastal bird photography in Morocco is perfect for photographers who love waterbirds, seabirds, and wetland species. Morocco’s Atlantic coastline stretches for thousands of kilometers and includes lagoons, estuaries, sandy beaches, and protected national parks. These coastal habitats attract both resident and migratory birds, especially during winter and spring seasons.</p>
<p>One of the most famous places for coastal bird photography in Morocco is Souss-Massa National Park near Agadir. This area is well known for the Northern Bald Ibis, one of the rarest birds in the world. Photographing this endangered species in its natural habitat is a dream for many bird photographers. The park also hosts herons, egrets, cormorants, and many waders.</p>
<p>Oualidia Lagoon is another excellent bird photography destination in Morocco. It is famous for flamingos, spoonbills, and different shorebirds. Calm water reflections make beautiful compositions, especially during sunrise. Essaouira and its coastal areas are also good for gulls, terns, and migratory seabirds.</p>
<p>Coastal bird photography tours in Morocco are ideal because of the soft ocean light, open views, and high bird activity. The mix of cliffs, wetlands, and sandy beaches allows photographers to capture different backgrounds in one area.</p>
<p>For bird photographers looking for diversity, rare species, and dramatic coastal scenery, Morocco offers one of the best bird photography experiences in Africa.</p>
</div>
</div>
